      "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "Sea bean is a brown algae of shallow waters in the infra-littoral zone of the English Channel, the North Sea, and the North Atlantic.</p><p> Olive to brown in colour, it measures up to 3 m. Its body is composed of a vegetative part: a very short stipe, located above its fixing clamp, bears a mushroom-shaped cupule. This cupule gives rise in spring to two straps, which are its reproductive part. This matrix is repeated several times.",
